{
  "$comment": "#EXP-2024: the live view of an agent's space on Exponential Desktop (f5-f6-design.md section 6 on #EXP-1514), a pure projection replayed in TS (src/spaces.ts) and Rust (uicore-model spaces.rs); the shell feeds it as `/spaces` (the taskbar's Agent spaces button and its list) and `/spaceView` (the pinned view). ROWS (`spaceRows(spaces, sessions) -> [{id, session, number, title, subtitle}]`, the `rows` cases {name, spaces, sessions, expected}): `spaces` = the compositor's ListSpaces ({id, session}: a space's id is `space-<n>`, n its number, counted up and never reused; `session` = the session its grant names), `sessions` = the session rows the shell's signed-in accounts hold ({id, title, parentId, rootId}, the title already resolved the way every client resolves it from what this machine can read: #EDE-194, a sealed title opens with the keyrings of the account's installs on this machine, the app's and the CLI daemon's, as a space's session runs on this machine and its host sealed it; `title` null or absent = no rung of session-title.json yields text, as for a sealed title and first prompt no keyring here opens: that fixture's `Untitled` never reaches a row). One row per space in the order of the NUMBERS (`space-2` before `space-10`; an id without a number after the numbered ones, by id). `number` = n (1 to 15 digits), null without one (or with more). `title` = its session's title, trimmed of white space (Unicode's White_Space and JavaScript's, U+FEFF and U+0085 too); a session no account holds (another account's, a teammate's private one on a shared device, a space made by hand), an empty title or none (it cannot be read) = `copy.untitled` with {n} = the number (the whole id without one). `subtitle` = a child session's chat (parentId set): its root's title (rootId, trimmed), null for a root session, for a root no account holds and for one whose title is empty or cannot be read. NO state word (the product's Working outlives a dead host; the picture is the state). The count (the button shows while it is above 0) = the number of spaces. VIEW (`spaceView(space, display, large) -> {width, height, picture: {width, height}, pixels: {width, height}, large, canGrow}`, the `view` cases {name, space, display, large, expected}): the pinned view is a box at the bottom right of the FIRST display above the taskbar: inside a `constants.border` px border, `constants.header` px of header (the title, the size and the close button) over the picture. `space` = the space's output size {width, height}; `display` = the first display's logical size and scale {width, height, scale}. The picture's width = min(`constants.maxWidth`, floor(display width / 3)); `large` asks for twice that, granted only where it fits (canGrow): the box at twice the width within display width - 2 x shell-layout.json panelMargin, and its height within display height - taskbarHeight - 2 x panelMargin. A box that does not fit that height is narrowed until it does (floor). The picture's height = round(width x space height / space width) (the space's aspect; a space of no size = 16:10); the box (`width`, `height`, the layer's size) = the picture + 2 x border wide, header + picture + 2 x border tall. `pixels` = the picture's box times the display's scale, rounded: what the capture is shrunk to, so the picture stays sharp at 1.5 and 2 (never bigger than the space itself: the shrink never scales up). TRAY (#EDE-266, `cuTray(input) -> {count, badge, list, rows, selected, menu}`, the `tray` cases {name, input, expected}): the taskbar's computer-use status icon replaces the Agent spaces button and its list (shown while count > 0). input = {rows (spaceRows' output), selected (the space the person picked in the popup; absent or no longer listed = the first row), controls ({spaceId: agent | paused | person}, the compositor's `control` of each space, absent = agent), sessions (the holder's `sessions` feed: {id = the chat, stop = its working sessions, trace}), watching (the session whose view is pinned)}. badge = `copy.spaceOne` / `copy.spaceMany` with {n}, empty without spaces; list = more than one space (the popup shows the rows above the tile, a press picks one; each row's `selected`). selected = the picked row plus: control; state = {label copy[control], icon, variant} (`constants.trayIcons`, `trayVariants`: Live, Paused, Taken over); trace = the steps of its session = the feed entry whose id is the space's session or whose stop holds it, its last `constants.trayTrace` lines; now = the title of the newest running line, else null; watching = its session is the pinned one; watch = Watch, or Stop watching while watching; pause = Pause while the agent drives, Resume while paused, null while taken over; take = Take over, or Hand back while taken over; each action {label, icon, value} (value = the copy key the press sends: `ede_cu {action: value, space}`). menu (the applet menu, a right click) = watch, pause (when not null), take, a separator, Stop (destructive); empty without a selection. THE SHELL: Stop = DestroySpace (the space ends, never its session); Watch pins the space's view (`ede_space`), Stop watching unpins it; Pause / Resume = the compositor's `control_space` paused / agent (the space's grant's input is refused `conflict` until then, observation never is); Take over pins the view and sets `person` with the view's picture rect: the person's pointer over the picture and, after a press in it, their keys (the compositor's bindings first) go to the space's seat; Hand back = agent; closing the view while taken over = paused (the agent never gets the space back unasked). A space never takes the hold (L-39). The popup's live tile is the pinned view's picture size capture of the selected space; the popup's namespace (`SPACE_TRAY_NAMESPACE`) is black in captures of the person's output. STOPPED (#EDE-272): the tray's Stop also parks the session's computer use until the person allows it again (the compositor's `park_session`; the park lives in the compositor, so a holder's restart keeps it and a compositor's ends it with the spaces): input `stopped` = the parked sessions [{session, title, subtitle}] (the shell resolves title and subtitle as a row's: its session's title, trimmed; a child's chat), oldest first. expected `stopped` = each with its title trimmed (empty or null = `copy.stoppedUntitled`) plus `allow` = {label copy.allow, icon, value: `allow`} (the popup's button sends `ede_cu {action: allow, session}`); `shown` = count > 0 or a stopped session (the status icon shows while it is true; the popup without spaces shows only the stopped rows). menu = the selected space's items, then (a separator first when there are some) one `copy.allow` item per stopped session with its title as `detail` and value `allow:<session>`. THE AGENT: while parked, the session's space grant's create_space and its driving ops are `conflict` in words starting `stopped by user`; ePilot answers that call with a tool error the agent explains to the person (no retry, no new space, how the person allows it again); after Allow the next call makes a new space.",
  "version": 1,
